#document(
  default_font = "Helvetica",
  default_size = pt(11),
  page = { size = "letter", orientation = "portrait" },
  margin = { top = pt(72), right = pt(72), bottom = pt(72), left = pt(72) }
)
#style(
  name = "Normal",
  type = "paragraph",
  run = { font = "Helvetica", size = pt(11) },
  paragraph = { spacing = { before = pt(0), after = pt(0), line = { rule = "exact", value = pt(20) } } }
)

PAGE FOOT: Word keeps a line at the foot of a page when the page holds the line less the space that a line multiple above one adds beneath its descender. The space before a paragraph must fit and the space after it need not. A table row must fit whole, and the foot of a column is the foot of a page. Each sample follows a filler line of exact height at the head of its page, once with the tallest filler that leaves the sample on the page and once with the shortest that moves it.

#style(
  name = "S1",
  type = "paragraph",
  based_on = "Normal",
  run = { font = "Helvetica", size = pt(11) },
  paragraph = { spacing = { before = pt(0), after = pt(0), line = { rule = "multiple", value = 1.0 } } }
)

#paragraph(page_break_before = true, spacing = { line = { rule = "exact", value = pt(634.75) } })[Filler 634.75.]

#paragraph(style = "S1")[Helvetica 11 multiple 1.0 below 634.75.]

#paragraph(page_break_before = true, spacing = { line = { rule = "exact", value = pt(634.85) } })[Filler 634.85.]

#paragraph(style = "S1")[Helvetica 11 multiple 1.0 below 634.85.]

